.TH MDE 1 "November 2026" "mde 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mde \- full-screen text-mode Markdown editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mde
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILENAME.md\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mde
is a specialized terminal text editor designed for editing and reading Markdown documents.
It supports real-time dual-pane split preview, in-place rich formatting, an active line
column ruler, persistent bottom shortcut key hint rows, interactive directory and file dialogue,
task checkboxes, smart list continuation, and multi-level undo/redo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage instructions and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print program version and build date.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save current file. Prompts for a file name if untitled.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open interactive file dialogue to browse directories and open a Markdown file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Save As interactive file dialogue to browse directories and select or type destination file name.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit mde. Prompts to save if unsaved changes exist.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+P " or " F2
Cycle view modes: Split View, In-Place Rich View, Fullscreen Rendered View. All modes support full editing and cursor tracking.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Toggle checkbox (\- [ ] <-> \- [x]) on the active line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Space
Set selection mark anchor. Move cursor with arrow keys, Ctrl+A, or Ctrl+E to extend the visual selection highlight.
.TP
.B Ctrl+X
Cut active selection to the clipboard (synced via OSC 52 to terminal/system clipboard).
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy active selection to the clipboard (synced via OSC 52).
.TP
.B Ctrl+V
Paste text from the clipboard at current cursor position.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Kill text from cursor to end of line, or join with next line if already at end of line.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+A " / " Home
Jump to beginning of current line.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+E " / " End
Jump to end of current line.
.TP
.BR Esc " / " Ctrl+G
Clear active selection mark.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Insert bold formatting markers (**) or wrap active selection.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Z " / " Ctrl+Y
Undo and Redo changes.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+F " / " F3
Search / find text in the document.
.TP
.BR F1 " or " Ctrl+H
Display the interactive two-tab help overlay (Tab 1: Editor Cheat Sheet, Tab 2: Markdown Syntax Guide).
.TP
.B Enter
Smart list auto-continuation. Hitting Enter on an empty list bullet cancels the list.
.TP
.BR Tab " / " Shift+Tab
Indent or unindent line by 2 spaces.
.TP
.B Ins
Toggle between Insert mode (steady block cursor) and Overwrite mode (steady underscore cursor). Cursor does not flash.
